# HOW TO USE: click "Send Request" above any line that starts with GET.
# The answer opens in a new tab on the right. The app must be running (mvn spring-boot:run).
# Each request has a ### title and a one-line note saying what it does.


################ DEMO 1: CHAT ################

### Demo 1: chat - ask the AI a question
# Sends your message to the AI and shows its full reply.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=Explain dependency injection in 3 lines

### Demo 1: chat - streaming
# Same idea, but the reply appears word by word, like ChatGPT typing.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat/stream?message=Write a haiku about Java

### Demo 1: chat - change the audience
# Same AI, different instructions: it explains recursion to a 10 year old.
GET http://localhost:8080/explain?topic=recursion&level=a 10 year old


################ EXERCISE 1: CHECK YOUR PERSONALITY ################

### Exercise 1: check your personality
# After you change defaultSystem in AiConfig.java and restart, send this. The answer should sound like your personality.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=Explain dependency injection in 3 lines


################ DEMO 2: STRUCTURED ANSWERS ################

### Demo 2: study plan
# Asks for a 5-day plan and gets it back as neat data (JSON) instead of plain text.
GET http://localhost:8080/study-plan?subject=Data Structures&days=5


################ EXERCISE 2: CHECK YOUR NEW FIELD ################

### Exercise 2: check the difficulty field
# After you add the difficulty field and restart, every task in the plan should have a "difficulty".
GET http://localhost:8080/study-plan?subject=Data Structures&days=5


################ DEMO 3: MEMORY AND TOOLS ################

### Demo 3: memory and tools (message 1)
# Tells the AI who you are and asks for free AI Lab slots. It uses the listFreeSlots tool.
GET http://localhost:8080/assistant?user=21BCE1234&message=My reg no is 21BCE1234. Which AI Lab slots are free?

### Demo 3: memory and tools (message 2)
# "The 2 PM one" only makes sense because the AI remembers message 1. It books with the bookSlot tool.
GET http://localhost:8080/assistant?user=21BCE1234&message=Book the 2 PM one for me

### Demo 3: a different student
# A different user id has its own memory, so the AI has no idea what was booked above.
GET http://localhost:8080/assistant?user=22BIT0042&message=What did I just book?


################ EXERCISE 3: CHECK YOUR CANCEL TOOL ################

### Exercise 3: cancel the booking
# After you add cancelBooking and restart, do the two Demo 3 requests first (to book 14:00), then send this.
GET http://localhost:8080/assistant?user=21BCE1234&message=Actually, cancel that booking.


################ DEMO 4: ANSWERING FROM DOCUMENTS (RAG) ################

### Demo 4: without the handbook
# The AI has never seen our handbook, so it guesses or says it does not know.
GET http://localhost:8080/ask/no-rag?question=What is the minimum attendance to sit for the final exam?

### Demo 4: with the handbook
# The app finds the right handbook piece first, so the AI answers correctly (82%).
GET http://localhost:8080/ask?question=What is the minimum attendance to sit for the final exam?

### Demo 4: another handbook question
# Another question the handbook can answer (re-evaluation fee).
GET http://localhost:8080/ask?question=How much does re-evaluation cost and is it refunded?


################ EXERCISE 4: CHECK YOUR NEW SECTION ################

### Exercise 4: ask about the canteen (with the handbook)
# After you add the Canteen section and restart, the AI should answer from it (open until 2 AM).
GET http://localhost:8080/ask?question=Until when is the canteen open during exams?

### Exercise 4: ask about the canteen (without the handbook)
# Same question without the handbook, to compare. The AI can only guess.
GET http://localhost:8080/ask/no-rag?question=Until when is the canteen open during exams?


################ TALK: WRITING GOOD PROMPTS (no exercise) ################

### Prompting: a vague prompt
# A vague request gets a vague answer.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=Write about Java streams.

### Prompting: a clear prompt
# A clear request (who, what, format, what to do when unsure) gets a much better answer.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=You are helping second-year students prepare for a viva. Explain Java streams in 5 short bullet points, with one 3-line code example. If you are not sure about something, say so.


################ BONUS: A SMALL AGENT (not in the live session) ################

### Bonus: give the AI a goal
# One goal, no steps. The AI decides to check free slots and then book one. Watch the terminal for TOOL EXECUTED.
GET http://localhost:8080/assistant?user=21BCE1234&message=Find me a free slot in the Cloud Lab after lunch and book it. My reg no is 21BCE1234.

### Bonus: same goal on a bigger model (port 8081)
# Only works if you started the app with the agent profile (see application-agent.yml).
GET http://localhost:8081/assistant?user=21BCE1234&message=Find me a free slot in the Cloud Lab after lunch and book it. My reg no is 21BCE1234.
